supermox-ve (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship /etc/init.d/supermox-sync and /usr/bin/supermox-sync: step 1 of the
    home folder sync in docs/shared-home.md. The init script runs one Syncthing
    instance per user in /etc/supermox/sync-users, as that user (start-stop-daemon
    --chuid), on 127.0.0.1:8384, :8385, ... each with its own state directory
    under /var/lib/supermox-sync/<user>. Once an instance answers on its API
    socket, supermox-sync reconcile applies this node's signed membership list
    to it: one device per member addressed over the WireGuard overlay
    (tcp://[<overlay_addr>]:22000), one folder per person, global discovery,
    local announcement, relays and NAT traversal off, staggered file versioning
    and the built-in .stignore. No member ever accepts a host by hand and no
    folder ever leaves the encrypted SuperMox network. supermox-sync status
    reports per folder: state, devices in sync, conflicts.
  * Depend on syncthing.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:20:00 +0000

supermox-ve (0.1.7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove debian/postinst. Its enable/start loop was a workaround for the
    pve services never getting S-links. The real fix is upstream: pve-manager's
    postinst/prerm now carry the #DEBHELPER# token (patch 0003-debhelper-token),
    so debhelper's dh_installinit inserts the update-rc.d/invoke-rc.d snippets
    and each package enables and starts its own services. supermox-ve no longer
    has to do it.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:45:00 +0000

supermox-ve (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship /etc/init.d/supermox-binfmt (debian/supermox-ve.supermox-binfmt.init,
    installed with dh_installinit --name=supermox-binfmt). It mounts binfmt_misc
    and feeds every binfmt.d/*.conf rule (usr/lib, /etc, /run; later directory
    wins) to the register file, skipping handlers already registered. Debian's
    qemu-user-binfmt only installs the conf files and relies on an init system
    that loads them, which sysvinit does not.
  * Recommend qemu-user-binfmt so foreign-architecture binaries (building or
    booting a rootfs for another architecture) work out of the box.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:15:00 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship /usr/sbin/supermox-node-caps: the per-node capability probe. It prints
    arch, kvm, lxc, tcg_targets, cpus and mem_mb (--json for machines) so a
    node can discover whether it is a KVM, TCG or LXC host. The probe is
    dependency-free (no dpkg, no systemd) so it also runs on Android/LineageOS.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:55:00 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on supermox-tmpfiles: qemu-server ships debian/tmpfiles, so
    debhelper's dh_installtmpfiles adds a "systemd-tmpfiles" dependency that
    Devuan satisfied with systemd-standalone-tmpfiles. Our package provides
    that virtual package without pulling in systemd.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:05:00 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop Conflicts: ifupdown. ifupdown2 provides ifupdown, so it made ifupdown2
    uninstallable; ifupdown2 already conflicts with the real ifupdown.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:08:16 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the networking init script (debian/supermox-ve.networking.init,
    installed with dh_installinit --name=networking --no-start) so ifupdown2
    brings up eth0 under sysvinit.
  * Declare Replaces: ifupdown and Conflicts: ifupdown so the package can
    take over the conffile left behind by ifupdown's own networking script.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:20:00 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Depend on cpio: proxmox-backup-file-restore's postinst runs it without
    declaring it.
  * Depend on ifupdown2 (pve-manager allows ifenslave as an alternative, but
    libpve-network-perl needs ifupdown2 outright): SuperMox ships its own
    networking init script for ifupdown2 so eth0 comes up under sysvinit.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:46:06 -0700

supermox-ve (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Metapackage replacing the upstream virtualization metapackage:
    depends on sysvinit-core and a Debian kernel package, conflicts
    with systemd-sysv and systemd, and provides the upstream package
    name so it can stand in for it.

